{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "MosaicAerosolPhaseState",
    "description": "MOSAIC's phase state of ONE size bin: SUBROUTINE aerosol_phase_state of chem/module_mosaic_therm.F (WRF v4.8.0), with the branch decisions of SUBROUTINE mesa, do_full_deliquescence / adjust_liquid_aerosol / adjust_solid_aerosol, calculate_kelvin, drh_mutual and aerosol_water_up. ASTEM calls it for every bin at the start of each of its sub-steps, after conform_electrolytes has rebuilt the bin's total electrolytes; it decides whether the bin is solid, liquid or mixed, how much water it holds, and the Kelvin factors that raise the equilibrium vapour pressures of HNO3, HCl, NH3 over a small droplet.\n\nINPUTS a consumer supplies: rh_pc, t_k, the bin's number concentration, the total species and the total electrolytes (as conform_electrolytes left them), and water_a_hyst -- the water the bin carried on the upper hysteresis leg at the end of the previous MOSAIC step (0 on the lower leg).\n\nDRY MASS AND VOLUME. sum_a A_a mw_a (and A_a mw_a / rho_a), plus the charge-balance H+ aer_H = (2 SO4 + NO3 + Cl + MSA + 2 CO3) - (2 Ca + Na + NH4), which the Fortran adds as nmol straight into the ng and ncc sums (an implied 1 g/mol and 1 g/cm3, written as such in mosaic_phase_parameters.esm), times 1e-15.\n\nTHE BRANCH (SUBROUTINE mesa, template mesa_path), tried in this order at the current water activity x: (1) x < crh = 0.35 and X_T > 1 or X_T < 0 and neither Ca(NO3)2 nor CaCl2 above ptol_mol_astem = 0.01 mol percent: effloresced, ALL SOLID. (2) water_a_hyst > 0.5 water_a_up, where water_a_up is the ZSR water of the totals at a fixed a_w = 0.6 without the kappa term (mhyst_method = uporlo_waterhyst): the upper hysteresis leg, FULLY LIQUID, water = ZSR water of the TOTAL electrolytes at x. (6) 0 < X_T < 1, the excess-sulfate domain: handed to mesa_ptc. (4) no salt above ptol_mol_astem: ALL SOLID -- which includes a pure H2SO4 or a purely carbonaceous bin on the lower leg. (5) x*100 below the mutual deliquescence RH of the salts present (jsulf_poor/jsulf_rich of the salt code, drh_mutual's cubic in T plus 1, or 10% for Ca(NO3)2/CaCl2 mixtures): ALL SOLID. (6) otherwise mesa_ptc. MESA_PTC, the pseudo-transient solid-liquid equilibrium solver (mixed phases), IS NOT TRANSCRIBED HERE: where the branch is 6, only `path` (and the inputs-only water_up and mass_dry) mean anything. The Fortran's step-2 'negative water' exit cannot occur with non-negative amounts and is omitted.\n\nTHE KELVIN EQUILIBRIUM. On the liquid branch the wet volume V = vol_dry + 1e-3 W(x), the volume-mean diameter Dp = (6 V/(N pi))^(1/3), the solution tension sigma = sigma_water + 49 (1 - x), and K = 1 + t(1 + t/2 (1 + t/3)) with t = 72 sigma/(R T Dp) (R = 8.3144e7) give the water activity the curved surface allows, x' = rh_pc 0.01/K(x) (`aw_next`). The bin's water activity is the FIXED POINT x = x'(x): written here as its residual `kelvin_residual` = aw0/K(x) - x, a function of the state x = `ah2o_a`, which is an input. Every other output is evaluated at that x. aerosol_phase_state finds the fixed point by plain fixed-point iteration from x = aw0, stopping when |x' - x|/x <= 1e-2 (1e-6 above 99% RH) or after ten updates; that iteration, its tolerance, its cap and its pass counter are a numerical solver, not physics, and are not written here (CLAUDE.md: .esm files never implement a numerical solver). EarthSciIntegrator solves kelvin_residual = 0 for ah2o_a (a scalar `solve` node; see data/eqwefic/notes/mosaic_mesa_kelvin_solvers.md, which also measures how far the Fortran's 1e-2 stop leaves it from the root). Because the branch is decided at x, a bin just above crh can be liquid at aw0 and solid at aw0/K(aw0) < crh: then the residual has no root (liquid gives K > 1 and wants x < crh; solid gives K = 1 and wants x = aw0), and the Fortran's answer -- solid, at the lowered x, with the first iterate's K left in kelvin(ibin) -- is an artefact of where its iteration stopped.\n\nOUTPUTS, at the state ah2o_a. aw_next and kelvin_residual, path, state (jaerosolstate; 0 where mesa_ptc decides), jhyst (jhyst_leg), water, mass/vol wet, dpmv, sigma_soln, kelvin, kel(gas) for H2SO4, HNO3, HCl, NH3, MSA (t = 4 sigma vbar/(R T Dp), 1 when solid), and the solid/liquid partition of species and electrolytes (liquid: all but CaSO4 and CaCO3 dissolve, Ca++ in the liquid is the Ca(NO3)2 + CaCl2; solid: everything stays solid). dpmv, sigma_soln, mass_wet and vol_wet are meaningful on the liquid branch only: on a solid exit the Fortran leaves whatever the previous pass, or the previous call, put there.\n\nFORTRAN_BUGS B29: sigma_water = 0.2358 tau^1.256 (1 - 0.625 tau) is the IAPWS surface tension of water in N/m (about 0.072), and calculate_kelvin adds it to 49 (1 - a_w), a term in dyn/cm; pure water's 72 dyn/cm enters as 0.072. The solution tension, and so every Kelvin factor, is too small: at 290 K and a_w = 0.6 it is 19.7 instead of 93.3 dyn/cm (every Kelvin term 4.7 times too small), and toward a_w = 1 it falls to 0.073 instead of 73 (a thousandfold). Reproduced as written; fixing it fails 65 assertions.\n\nPRECISION. Double-precision arithmetic with the default-real literals at their binary32 values (mosaic_phase_parameters.esm): 0.35, 0.01, 0.6, 1e-15, 1e-3, 3.1415926, 1./3. (formed in REAL), 647.15, 0.2358, 1.256, 1e-2, 1e-6. rh_pc itself is 100*relhumclm formed in default REAL.\n\nTESTS AND COVERAGE. Eleven calls from the chem170 aerosol_phase_state capture (dumps/chem170_mosaic_phase, WRF fork e277517c; reference namelist unchanged, fields shared with dumps/chem170_mosaic_therm bit-identical): the upper leg with one and two Kelvin passes, efflorescence below crh, lower-leg bins below their mutual DRH, and three mesa_ptc hand-offs (mass-converged, flux-converged and NOT converged in 80 iterations). Of the column's 15104 recorded calls, 6892 take the upper leg, 446 effloresce, 3692 sit below their mutual DRH, and 4074 go to mesa_ptc (206 of them unconverged); 1020 need a second Kelvin pass and none a third. A sweep of 480 non-mesa_ptc calls sampled across all 16 steps (not kept as tests) agreed bit for bit in 38055 of 39264 assertions and to 5.4e-15 relative at worst (water). Plus 14 hand-specified bins run through WRF's own compiled aerosol_phase_state (kernels/mosaic_therm_driver mode 2; chem170_scm/therm64/make_cases.py) for what the column does not show: liquid at 0.30 (Ca blocks efflorescence), 0.90 and 0.995 (the 1e-6 tolerance, three passes); efflorescence on the SECOND pass; the no-salt solids (H2SO4, carbon); ammonium sulfate and NaCl + NH4NO3 below their DRH. Every call is evaluated at the water activity the Fortran's Kelvin iteration STOPPED at (its final ah2o_a, an input here), where kelvin_residual is the update its tolerance declined to apply; a call that took a second pass is evaluated as well at its FIRST iterate aw0, where aw_next must be the second iterate the Fortran moved to (and, for the hand bin that effloresces on its second pass, kelvin is the first iterate's K the Fortran leaves in kelvin(ibin)). The 0.995 bin's middle iterate is not taped, so it is tested at its final iterate only. All at rel 1e-9 (the residual, a difference of two O(1) numbers, with an absolute floor of 1e-14), integer flags exactly. The Fortran's stopping point is NOT a target: data/eqwefic/notes/mosaic_mesa_kelvin_solvers.md measures it against the converged root (median 1.9e-3, worst 1.0e-2 relative in ah2o_a; 1.6e-2 in the water). Mutation-checked (2026-11-12, after the iteration was removed): fixing B29 fails 78, aw_next formed from ah2o_a instead of aw0 5, K = 1 everywhere 24, a second-order Kelvin series 57, the residual's sign 18. (Before the rework, on the driver bins: crh = 0.30 failed 14, the double-precision pi 9 and 1/3 44, dropping aer_H from the dry mass 14.) The 63 mutual-DRH curves are pinned as a whole table (mdrh_table, the drh_mutual cubic at t_k) at six temperatures from 240 to 315 K through the driver (chem170_scm/therm64/mdrh) and at the column's top-level temperature from the capture, 63 assertions each (tools/fill_mosaic_mdrh_table_tests.py); perturbing any curve's leading coefficient by 1e-4 fails all seven. NOT covered: a bin whose ZSR water is exactly zero on the upper leg (aerosol_water then flags it all solid from inside the liquid branch).",
    "authors": [
      "EqWeFiC"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Zaveri, R.A., Easter, R.C., Fast, J.D., Peters, L.K. (2008). Model for Simulating Aerosol Interactions and Chemistry (MOSAIC). J. Geophys. Res. 113, D13204."
      },
      {
        "citation": "WRF v4.8.0 chem/module_mosaic_therm.F"
      }
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NEL": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 22,
      "description": "Number of MOSAIC electrolytes carried (nelectrolyte is 23; the 23rd, joc, is never assigned and stays zero)."
    },
    "NZSR": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 19,
      "description": "Electrolytes that hold water, the first nsalt + 4."
    },
    "NSALT": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 15,
      "description": "Soluble salts nsalt, the electrolytes MESA's salt-combination code counts."
    },
    "NAER": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 112,
      "description": "MOSAIC aerosol species per bin (naer, chem_opt = 170 build)."
    }
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "el": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NEL"
    },
    "aer": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NAER"
    },
    "pc": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 6
    },
    "gas": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 5
    },
    "mdrhcurve": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 63
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "MosaicAerosolPhaseState": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "./mosaic_thermo_templates.esm"
        }
      ],
      "subsystems": {
        "tp": {
          "ref": "./mosaic_thermo_parameters.esm"
        },
        "pp": {
          "ref": "./mosaic_phase_parameters.esm"
        }
      },
      "expression_templates": {
        "mesa_path": {
          "params": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Which branch of SUBROUTINE mesa decides the bin at water activity x: 1 below the crystallization point (x < crh and crh_ok), all solid; 2 the upper hysteresis leg, fully deliquesced (liquid); 6 the excess-sulfate domain 0 < X_T < 1, or a salt mixture at or above its mutual deliquescence point, handed to mesa_ptc (NOT transcribed here); 4 no salt present, all solid; 5 below the mutual deliquescence point, all solid. Reads the consumer's crh_ok, upper_leg, x_t, salt_code and mdrh.",
          "body": {
            "op": "ifelse",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "and",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "<",
                    "args": [
                      "x",
                      "pp.crh"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": ">",
                    "args": [
                      "crh_ok",
                      0.5
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              1.0,
              {
                "op": "ifelse",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": ">",
                    "args": [
                      "upper_leg",
                      0.5
                    ]
                  },
                  2.0,
                  {
                    "op": "ifelse",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "and",
                        "args": [
                          {
                            "op": "<",
                            "args": [
                              "x_t",
                              1.0
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "op": ">",
                            "args": [
                              "x_t",
                              0.0
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      6.0,
                      {
                        "op": "ifelse",
                        "args": [
                          {
                            "op": "==",
                            "args": [
                              "salt_code",
                              0.0
                            ]
                          },
                          4.0,
                          {
                            "op": "ifelse",
                            "args": [
                              {
                                "op": "<",
                                "args": [
                                  {
                                    "op": "*",
                                    "args": [
                                      "x",
                                      100.0
                                    ]
                                  },
                                  "mdrh"
                                ]
                              },
                              5.0,
                              6.0
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "wet_volume": {
          "params": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Wet volume vol_dry + 1e-3 W(x) of the fully deliquesced bin at water activity x, cm3 per cm3 of air.",
          "body": {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              "vol_dry",
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "apply_expression_template",
                    "args": [],
                    "name": "zsr_water",
                    "bindings": {
                      "a": "x"
                    }
                  },
                  "pp.water_to_g_per_cm3"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "wet_diameter": {
          "params": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Volume-mean wet diameter (6 V/(N pi))^(1/3) (calculate_kelvin), cm, with pi and 1/3 at their binary32 values.",
          "body": {
            "op": "^",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "/",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      6.0,
                      {
                        "op": "apply_expression_template",
                        "args": [],
                        "name": "wet_volume",
                        "bindings": {
                          "x": "x"
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      "num",
                      "pp.pi_k"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              "pp.third"
            ]
          }
        },
        "solution_tension": {
          "params": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Solution surface tension sigma_water + 49 (1 - x) (calculate_kelvin), with the B29 unit slip in sigma_water.",
          "body": {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              "sigma_water",
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  49.0,
                  {
                    "op": "-",
                    "args": [
                      1.0,
                      "x"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "kelvin_series": {
          "params": [
            "t"
          ],
          "description": "MOSAIC's third-order expansion of exp(t): 1 + t (1 + t/2 (1 + t/3)).",
          "body": {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              1.0,
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  "t",
                  {
                    "op": "+",
                    "args": [
                      1.0,
                      {
                        "op": "*",
                        "args": [
                          0.5,
                          "t",
                          {
                            "op": "+",
                            "args": [
                              1.0,
                              {
                                "op": "/",
                                "args": [
                                  "t",
                                  3.0
                                ]
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "kelvin_factor": {
          "params": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Kelvin factor of the fully deliquesced bin at water activity x: the series of 72 sigma/(R T Dp), R = 8.3144e7 erg/(mol K).",
          "body": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "kelvin_series",
            "bindings": {
              "t": {
                "op": "/",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      72.0,
                      {
                        "op": "apply_expression_template",
                        "args": [],
                        "name": "solution_tension",
                        "bindings": {
                          "x": "x"
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      "pp.r_cgs",
                      "t_k",
                      {
                        "op": "apply_expression_template",
                        "args": [],
                        "name": "wet_diameter",
                        "bindings": {
                          "x": "x"
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "rh_pc": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "percent",
          "default": 60.0,
          "description": "Relative humidity in percent, rh_pc = 100.*relhumclm(k), formed by mosaic() in default REAL and held in real(kind=8); every water activity below starts from rh_pc*0.01."
        },
        "t_k": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K",
          "default": 290.0,
          "description": "Air temperature t_k."
        },
        "num": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/cm^3",
          "default": 1000.0,
          "description": "Bin number concentration num_a(ibin), particles per cm3 of air."
        },
        "aer_t": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Total species amounts aer(ja, jtotal, ibin) after conform_electrolytes, nmol per m3 of air.",
          "shape": [
            "aer"
          ]
        },
        "elec": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Total electrolyte amounts electrolyte(je, jtotal, ibin) as conform_electrolytes left them, nmol per m3 of air.",
          "shape": [
            "el"
          ]
        },
        "water_hyst": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "water_a_hyst(ibin): the water the bin carried on the upper hysteresis leg at the end of the previous MOSAIC step (mosaic_dynamic_solver), or 0 on the lower leg."
        },
        "ah2o_a": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.5,
          "description": "THE STATE: the bin water activity ah2o_a(ibin) at which the phase state is evaluated -- the unknown of the Kelvin equilibrium x = aw0/K(x) (see kelvin_residual). On the tape, an iterate of aerosol_phase_state's loop (its final value, or the first iterate aw0)."
        },
        "aer_h": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "The H+ implied by charge balance of the totals, (2 SO4 + NO3 + Cl + MSA + 2 CO3) - (2 Ca + Na + NH4); the Fortran adds this nmol amount straight into the ng and ncc sums, i.e. at an implied 1 g/mol and 1 g/cm3."
        },
        "mass_dry": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "g/cm^3",
          "description": "Dry mass of the bin mass_dry_a, g per cm3 of air."
        },
        "vol_dry": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Dry volume of the bin vol_dry_a, cm3 of particle per cm3 of air."
        },
        "v_kappa": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol*cm^3/(mol*m^3)",
          "description": "kappa-weighted dry volume of the non-electrolytes, read by the zsr_water template (as in aerosol_water_zsr.esm)."
        },
        "water_up": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "description": "aerosol_water_up: the ZSR water of the TOTAL electrolytes at a fixed water activity 0.6 (binary32), no kappa term and no fit-range clamp (bin_molality_60), each term scaled by 1e-9 before summing."
        },
        "upper_leg": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1 where water_a_hyst > 0.5 water_a_up (mhyst_method = uporlo_waterhyst): MESA forces the bin onto the upper (fully deliquesced) branch."
        },
        "x_t": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "calculate_xt on the totals: (NH4 + Na + 2 Ca)/(SO4 + MSA/2), or -1 without sulfate or MSA."
        },
        "elec_sum": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Sum of the total electrolytes, or 1 where it is zero (MESA's guard)."
        },
        "epercent": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "percent",
          "description": "Mole percent of each electrolyte in the total, 100 E_e / sum E.",
          "shape": [
            "el"
          ]
        },
        "crh_ok": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1 where the composition allows efflorescence at the crystallization point: X_T > 1 or X_T < 0, and neither Ca(NO3)2 nor CaCl2 above ptol_mol_astem percent."
        },
        "salt_code": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "MESA's salt-combination code: the sum of jsalt_index over the salts present above ptol_mol_astem percent (0: none)."
        },
        "mdrh_index": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Index of the salt combination's mutual deliquescence curve: jsulf_poor(code) where X_T >= 2 or X_T < 0, else jsulf_rich(code); 0 where no salt is present."
        },
        "mdrh": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "percent",
          "description": "Mutual deliquescence relative humidity of the bin's salt combination: curve mdrh_index of mdrh_table (0 without a salt)."
        },
        "sigma_water": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "dyn/cm",
          "description": "Surface tension of pure water as update_thermodynamic_constants forms it, 0.2358 tau^1.256 (1 - 0.625 tau), tau = (647.15 - T)/647.15. THE FORMULA GIVES N/m (about 0.072) and calculate_kelvin adds it to a term in dyn/cm (FORTRAN_BUGS B29); reproduced as written, so this is 1000 times too small for the dyn/cm it is used as."
        },
        "aw0": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "The ambient water activity ah2o = rh_pc*0.01 (binary32 0.01): the water activity a particle with no Kelvin effect would have."
        },
        "path": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "The MESA branch at water activity ah2o_a (see mesa_path). 6 means mesa_ptc decides the phase (mesa_salt_equilibrium.esm), which this component does not evaluate: none of its other outputs is meaningful there."
        },
        "liquid": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1 where the bin ends fully liquid (path 2)."
        },
        "state": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "jaerosolstate: 2 all liquid (path 2), 1 all solid (paths 1, 4, 5), 0 where mesa_ptc decides (path 6, not transcribed)."
        },
        "jhyst": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "jhyst_leg on exit: 1 (upper) when liquid, 0 (lower) when solid."
        },
        "water": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "description": "Liquid water water_a: the ZSR water of the total electrolytes at ah2o_a when liquid, 0 when solid."
        },
        "mass_wet": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "g/cm^3",
          "description": "Wet mass mass_dry + 1e-3 water (meaningful when liquid; on a solid exit the Fortran leaves the previous pass's value)."
        },
        "vol_wet": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Wet volume vol_dry + 1e-3 water (as mass_wet)."
        },
        "dpmv": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "cm",
          "description": "Volume-mean wet diameter of the liquid bin at ah2o_a."
        },
        "sigma_soln": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "dyn/cm",
          "description": "Solution surface tension at the final water activity."
        },
        "kelvin": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Kelvin factor kelvin(ibin) at ah2o_a: K(ah2o_a) when liquid, 1 otherwise (no curved liquid surface). (On a solid exit the Fortran leaves the PREVIOUS iterate's K in kelvin(ibin), an artefact of its loop; the tests assert that value at the previous iterate, where it belongs.)"
        },
        "kel": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Kelvin factors of the condensing gases kel(iv), iv = H2SO4, HNO3, HCl, NH3, MSA: the series of 4 sigma vbar_iv/(R T Dp) when liquid; 1 when solid.",
          "shape": [
            "gas"
          ]
        },
        "elec_l": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Liquid electrolytes: when liquid every total except CaSO4 and CaCO3, which stay solid; 0 when solid.",
          "shape": [
            "el"
          ]
        },
        "elec_s": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Solid electrolytes: the totals less the liquid.",
          "shape": [
            "el"
          ]
        },
        "aer_l": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Liquid species aer(:, jliquid): when liquid, SO4 less the CaSO4, NO3, Cl, NH4, MSA and Na in full, Ca as the dissolved Ca(NO3)2 + CaCl2, everything else 0; 0 when solid.",
          "shape": [
            "aer"
          ]
        },
        "aer_s": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "nmol/m^3",
          "description": "Solid species aer(:, jsolid): when liquid, SO4 as CaSO4, Ca as CaCO3 + CaSO4, the ions NO3 Cl NH4 MSA Na at 0 and every other species in full; the totals when solid.",
          "shape": [
            "aer"
          ]
        },
        "mdrh_table": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "percent",
          "shape": [
            "mdrhcurve"
          ],
          "description": "The 63 mutual deliquescence relative humidities at t_k, mdrh_t(1:63) as update_thermodynamic_constants fills them (drh_mutual): 10 for the Ca(NO3)2/CaCl2 mixtures (curves 7, 8, 34-51), else the cubic d_1 + T(d_2 + T(d_3 + T d_4)) + 1. MESA reads the one curve of the bin's salt combination (mdrh)."
        },
        "aw_next": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "The water activity the Kelvin equation gives back for this state, aw0/K(ah2o_a) (ah2o_a_new of aerosol_phase_state's loop): the map whose fixed point is the bin's water activity."
        },
        "kelvin_residual": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "THE RESIDUAL of the Kelvin equilibrium, aw0/K(ah2o_a) - ah2o_a: zero at the bin's equilibrium water activity. On the liquid branch K depends on ah2o_a through the ZSR water, so this is a scalar nonlinear equation in ah2o_a; on a solid branch K = 1 and the root is ah2o_a = aw0. Meaningless on path 6 (mesa_ptc decides, and its water is mesa_salt_equilibrium's)."
        }
      },
